{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And she shall remove her captive's garment.</b> Because they are beautiful — the gentiles adorn their daughters for war in order to entice others to lie with them (Sifrei)." "<b>And she shall sit in your house.</b> In the house he uses — he enters and encounters her, he goes out and encounters her, he sees her weeping, he sees her dishevelment, so that she becomes loathsome to him (Sifrei)." "<b>And she shall weep for her father.</b> All this — why? So that an Israelite daughter be joyful while this one is sorrowful; an Israelite daughter adorns herself while this one grows dishevelled (there)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:53.803477748Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}